# Writes one file into the run folder of this run. Returns '' on success, a protocol note otherwise.
# A failed write never ends the run. cRunFolder is set by $runExecutor; the line below is a fallback.
# The folder is made by the static FileOps (its return is an error code, so the file system is asked),
# the file is written through the FileOps object, which has no $createdir (lore 7.7).
If len(cRunFolder)=0
	Calculate cRunFolder as $cinst.$runFolderPath()
End If
Do FileOps.$createdir(cRunFolder,kTrue)
If FileOps.$doesfileexist(cRunFolder)
Else
	Quit method con('[folder] could not be created at [',cRunFolder,'] - nothing written. ')
End If
Do iFileOps.$createfile(con(cRunFolder,pName)) Returns ok
If ok
	Do iFileOps.$writecharacter(kUniTypeUTF8,pText,kFalse,kFalse) Returns ok
	Do iFileOps.$closefile()
	If ok
		Quit method ''
	End If
End If
Do iFileOps.$getlasterror(errText) Returns errCode
Quit method con('[file] ',pName,' FAILED: ',errText,' ')